## [2.1.20260904162413] - 2026-09-04 16:24:13

### ADD

- Added **ALPN** field support: node links now automatically carry an ALPN parameter, adapting to more client scenarios.

### Debug

- Fixed **HTTPS proxy**: handshake failure when the upstream server requested a client certificate (CertificateRequest); an empty certificate is now sent back to complete the handshake normally. [Commit](https://github.com/cmliu/CF-Workers-CheckSocks5/commit/ae93bc28462a6df03795143a5caa85f717ba231a)

## [2.1.20260811144522] - 2026-08-11 14:45:22

### Change

- Optimized **XHTTP** uplink transport: added a data-packing mechanism, small chunks are merged before being sent as one, reducing frequent small-packet writes, lowering resource overhead, and making large-file uploads smoother.

## [2.1.20260810030901] - 2026-08-10 03:09:01

### ADD

- Added **XHTTP obfs padding** receiver-side support: recognizes the `xPaddingObfsMode` (tokenish / queryInHeader) obfuscation header.

## [2.1.20260809231057] - 2026-08-09 23:10:57

### Debug

- Fixed **XHTTP chain proxy** parameter parsing: a trailing `/` at the end of the path used to break the reverse-proxy config; trailing slashes are now handled correctly.

## [2.1.20260809201158] - 2026-08-09 20:11:58

### Change

- Optimized **XHTTP** transport pipeline: TCP data now flows directly both ways via `request.body.pipeTo(socket.writable)` and `socket.readable.pipeTo(IdentityTransformStream)`, no longer going through the ReadableStream + uplink write queue + BYOB/Grain chunk-by-chunk relay, significantly reducing CPU usage.
- Optimized **XHTTP** connection management: `forwardataTCP` gained an "establish connection only" mode — after connecting and writing the first packet it returns the socket directly for the pipe to take over, while still keeping the fallback logic that automatically switches to the reverse proxy after a direct-connect failure (gRPC/WS callers are unaffected).
- Optimized **XHTTP UDP** handling: the UDP branch was split out into a dedicated handler function, preserving the Trojan UDP reverse-proxy and DNS forwarding logic.

## [2.1.20260729235734] - 2026-07-29 23:57:34

### Change

- Fixed the **PRELOAD_RACE_DIAL** environment variable logic: the default changed from `true` to `false` (preload race dial is now **disabled** by default); set it to `1` or `true` to **enable** it. Updated the README description of this variable accordingly. [Commit](https://github.com/cmliu/edgetunnel/commit/aea8b85688ef6066116af551cfd5e6fd2ce77567)

## [2.1.20260724150359] - 2026-07-24 15:03:59

### Change

- Synced the latest **GrainTCP** transport optimizations: the uplink Grain packing target was adjusted from `16KB` to `20KB`, reusing a unified collect/pack core; consecutive small chunks are opportunistically merged during the drain phase, reducing frequent `writer.write()` calls. [Upstream commit](https://github.com/ToiCF/GrainTCP/commit/1d22628f4d1413989f521f1d41591b0c72e658eb)
- Optimized downlink **GrainTCP** aggregation: kept the `32KB` aggregation cap, using a `tail × 12` low-water mark and up to `4` rounds of `1ms` growth observation each; flush can send multiple aggregated packets back to back, and sends promptly when nearing the cap, reducing the number of small WebSocket frames. [Upstream commit](https://github.com/ToiCF/GrainTCP/commit/1d22628f4d1413989f521f1d41591b0c72e658eb)
- Optimized downlink packet handling: large chunks are sent directly when Grain is empty, small chunks are first detached from the reusable read buffer on the BYOB/default reader path; aggregated results are copied before being sent, avoiding data corruption from scratch-buffer reuse. [Upstream commit](https://github.com/ToiCF/GrainTCP/commit/1d22628f4d1413989f521f1d41591b0c72e658eb)
- Strengthened TCP connection management based on the upstream transport model: added connection generation, socket identity, and an old-downlink drain barrier; during a redial, uplink data keeps being collected and waits for the new writer, so the async teardown of the old reader, timer, or connection can no longer contaminate the new connection. [Upstream approach](https://github.com/ToiCF/GrainTCP/commit/1d22628f4d1413989f521f1d41591b0c72e658eb)
- Unified the serial send chain for direct sends, segmented sends, and timed flushes based on the upstream Grain send model, and persisted async send errors; the response header is only consumed on the first real send, preventing a redial or a stale connection from prematurely consuming the protocol response header. [Upstream approach](https://github.com/ToiCF/GrainTCP/commit/1d22628f4d1413989f521f1d41591b0c72e658eb)
- Kept existing multi-protocol compatibility: WS uplink uses non-blocking enqueue to reduce message-handling stalls, while XHTTP/gRPC still wait for the remote write to complete; locally kept the `16MiB / 4096`-entry upload high-water protection to prevent unbounded growth of the Worker queue. [Upstream change](https://github.com/ToiCF/GrainTCP/commit/1d22628f4d1413989f521f1d41591b0c72e658eb)
- Optimized: the local speed-test response is now only enabled in **reverse-proxy mode**; when using a **SOCKS5/HTTP/HTTPS/TURN/SSTP** proxy, speed-test requests are forwarded normally instead.

## [2.1.20260722191426] - 2026-07-22 19:14:26

### Change

- Adapted to the `http://cp.cloudflare.com/generate_204` real-connectivity test address.

## [2.1.20260711190235] - 2026-07-11 19:02:35

### ADD

- Added the **TCP_CONCURRENT_DIAL** environment variable to customize the **TCP concurrent dial count**; once set, it no longer auto-downgrades to a single path on China Mobile networks.
- Added the **PROXY_CONCURRENT_DIAL** environment variable to customize the **reverse-proxy concurrent dial count**.

## [2.1.20260711022318] - 2026-07-11 02:23:18

### Change

- Optimized **reverse-proxy related logic**: fixed an issue where multi-reverse-proxy node parameters could be unexpectedly overwritten by global variables, causing them not to take effect.
- Optimized the **DoH cache**: caches recent domain resolution results to reduce repeated requests, speeding up resolution and lowering resource usage; domains with no resolution result are also cached temporarily to avoid repeated queries.

### ADD

- Added **reverse-proxy concurrent dial count**: lets you adjust the concurrency of reverse-proxy connections yourself. A higher concurrency means faster connections but more frequent IP switching; a lower concurrency makes the connection process more stable.
- Added **subscription conversion config**: more feature options, including **UDP**, **XUDP**, **TLS 1.3**, **insert node type**, and **basic node sorting**, all passed through to the subscription-conversion backend.
- Added **Trojan fallback proxy**: the Trojan protocol now supports configuring a fallback proxy address. When the primary connection is unreachable, it can automatically switch to the fallback proxy to keep working, making the connection more stable and reliable. [PR #1359](https://github.com/cmliu/edgetunnel/pull/1359)

