## [2.1.20260518183745] - 2026-05-18 18:37:45

### ADD

- Added the **PRELOAD_RACE_DIAL** environment variable to customize **TCP preload race dial**: on the first direct connection to a domain, A/AAAA records can be queried concurrently via DoH first, preferring IPv4 and filling in with IPv6 up to the `TCP concurrent dial count` cap when needed; the reverse-proxy failure fallback logic is separated from a normal first direct connection to avoid mistakenly triggering the preload.

## [2.1.20260517185203] - 2026-05-17 18:52:03

### Debug

- Fixed **WS/XHTTP/gRPC uploads**: uplink writes now wait for the remote write to complete before processing the next chunk, preventing data from piling up rapidly inside the Worker during upload bursts and triggering an `upload queue overflow`.
- Optimized the **WS explicit transport queue**: the uplink queue protection was changed from 256KB to 16MB / 4096 entries, and pending write tasks are now released correctly during queue cleanup, reducing occasional overflow during large-file uploads.

## [2.1.20260515185129] - 2026-05-15 18:51:29

### Change

- Optimized the **Shadowsocks subscription**: when TLS is disabled, the preferred port is now automatically rewritten to the noTLS port. (This does not apply to reverse-proxy IPs.)
- Optimized the **GO2SOCKS5** variable: changed from overwrite mode to append mode. [PR #1202](https://github.com/cmliu/edgetunnel/pull/1202)

## [2.1.20260513042803] - 2026-05-13 04:28:03

### Change

- Optimized the **VLESS** hot path: the UUID is pre-decoded into 16 bytes for direct comparison, and first-packet parsing now uses offsets and `subarray()` for a lower-copy approach. [Open-source reference](https://github.com/ToiCF/GrainTCP)
- Optimized **WS Early Data**: added an 8KB cap as protection, and avoided a regular WebSocket sub-protocol being mistaken for early data and injected into the first packet. [Open-source reference](https://github.com/ToiCF/GrainTCP)
- Optimized the **WS/XHTTP/gRPC** uplink path: added a bounded queue, small-packet merging, and 256KB back-pressure protection, reducing the frequency of small-packet writes and preventing unbounded queue growth. [Open-source reference](https://github.com/ToiCF/GrainTCP)
- Optimized the downlink **GrainTCP** send flow: small packets are aggregated using a microtask and a short quiet window, large packets flush the aggregator first and are then sent directly on the BYOB path, reducing copies and the number of WebSocket frames. [Open-source reference](https://github.com/ToiCF/GrainTCP)
- Optimized the TCP connection flow: direct-connect and proxyip reverse-proxy candidates now use 4-way concurrent dialing to race for the first successful connection, while SOCKS/HTTP/HTTPS/TURN/SSTP proxy chains keep their original handshake logic. [Open-source reference](https://github.com/ToiCF/GrainTCP)
- Optimized the WebSocket handshake and the main WS transport path: `allowHalfOpen` gained an exception fallback, the 101 response clears `Sec-WebSocket-Extensions`, and the main WS path now uses an explicit ordered queue. [Open-source reference](https://github.com/ToiCF/GrainTCP)

## [2.1.20260511041705] - 2026-05-11 04:17:05

### Change

- Improved the password validation logic on the **login settings page**, so that a newline character accidentally included when a beginner sets the `ADMIN` password no longer makes the password impossible to enter correctly (and their sanity along with it)!

### Delete

- Removed the request-count refresh countdown from the subscription response header, so beginners don't panic when they see it!

## [2.1.20260508190728] - 2026-05-08 19:07:28

### Debug

- Fixed an issue during **random preferred IP** selection where carrier info was dropped after subscription conversion, preventing the corresponding carrier's preferred IP from being generated.

### Change

- Optimized subscription conversion to submit a temporary `TOKEN` for the conversion, preventing the real subscription address from being leaked.

## [2.1.20260508041513] - 2026-05-08 04:15:13

### Change

- Optimized the **PROXYIP** domain resolution flow: for a domain, the reverse-proxy address is now read from the **TXT** record first, falling back to the **A** record result if no TXT result is obtained.
- When neither the TXT nor the A record yields a result, the **AAAA** record is then requested, reducing unnecessary IPv6 queries.

### Delete

- Removed the special-case handling for the `.william` domain and the Google DoH fallback-retry logic; regular domains can now also configure a reverse-proxy address via a TXT record.

